 "verdict": "consistent: short and extended four-like signs distinguish yāʾ and wāw in all eleven comparisons.",
 "notes": "A small black pendant with a leftward arm appears just above the divider before the yāʾ on 91r l.12. It matches the fāʾ of يصطفيك. Read both signs of في, giving 85 written signs. The double pointed sign is tāʾ in كنت, انت, تجي and consequently in يتقيك and يحتميك. The last reading restores the extra yāʾ before kāf. The three wāw signs extend their crossbars to the right of the upright, whereas all eight yāʾ signs stop at the upright. Final hamzas have no distinct sign in the five words previously identified.",
